claim.claim-text:
What is claimed is: 1. A spraying device comprising a housing 12 containing a top and bottom portion defining a chamber therein for fluid ingress and egress into said bottom portion wherein said housing includes an outer structure 18 containing an inner structure 16, and a tensioning device 22 which releasably positions said outer structure at said housing bottom; said inner structure 16 engaged to an arm member 20 for spraying said fluid, such that said inner structure causes said arm member to move in a linear and rotating relationship relative to housing; said outer structure 18 and inner structure 16 engaged to one another such that said outer structure 18 causes said inner structure to move in a linear and rotating relationship relative to said housing; wherein the ingress of fluid in said chamber causes said inner and outer structure to move linearly and wherein at a predetermined point the inner structure is prevented from moving in said linear direction while said outer structure continues to move linearly, thereby causing said inner structure to rotate. 2. The spraying device of claim 1 wherein said outer structure 18 and said inner structure 16 respectively comprise a male helical member 31 and female helical member 32. 3. The spraying device of claim 1, wherein said inner structure is prevented from moving in said linear direction by contacting said top portion of said housing. 4. The spraying device of claim 1 wherein said arm member includes a nozzle 52 connected to said arm member. 5. The spraying device if claim 1 wherein said tensioning device 22 comprises a spring. 6. The spraying device of claim 1 wherein said outer structure is mechanically engaged to said housing to restrict said outer structure rotation. 7. A spraying device for a headlamp or tailight-cleaning system for a motor vehicle comprising 

 a housing 12 containing a top and bottom portion defining a chamber therein for fluid ingress and egress into said bottom portion wherein said housing includes an outer structure 18 containing an inner structure 16, and a tensioning device 22 which releasably positions said outer structure at said housing bottom; said inner structure 16 engaged to an arm member 20 for spraying said fluid, such that said inner structure causes said arm member to move in a linear and rotating relationship relative to housing; said outer structure 18 and inner structure 16 engaged to one another such that said outer structure 18 causes said inner structure to move in a linear and rotating relationship relative to said housing; wherein the ingress of fluid in said chamber causes said inner and outer structure to move linearly and wherein at a predetermined point the inner structure is prevented from moving in said liner direction while said outer structure continues to move linearly, thereby causing said inner structure to rotate. 8. The spraying device system of claim 7, said device positioned within a bumper 40 of said motor vehicle. 9. The spraying device of claim 8, wherein said arm member 20 is flush mounted in said vehicle bumper. 10. The spraying device of claim 7, said device positioned proximate a headlamp or tail-lamp housing 50. 11. A method of selectively positioning an arm 20 containing a nozzle 52 to provide a spraying pattern on a given surface, said positioning achieved via a fluid-driven mechanical operation, wherein said mechanical-driven mechanical operation comprises: introducing fluid into a housing 12 containing a chamber for ingress and egress of fluid, wherein said chamber further contains a linearly displaceable inner structure 16 engaged with an outer linearly displaceable structure 18, said inner structure 16 also capable of rotational displacement; 

 said fluid ingress displacing said inner and outer structure in a linear direction followed by rotational displacement of said inner structure due to linear displacement of said outer structure. 12. The method of claim 11, wherein said inner structure is engaged to said arm, which arm undergoes both linear and rotational displacement. 13. The method of claim 11, whereupon removal of said fluid in said housing, said inner structure moves in a rotational direction and linear direction counter to the rotational and linear direction caused by fluid ingress.
